* kindling proof model
*
* 4 variables, 3 constraints
*
* --- x1 in [0, 1], the model's x1 ---
* x1 = 1*x1b0
*
* x1ge{v} means x1 >= v, in both directions at once.
* Each line is two constraints: _up is x1ge{v} ==> 1*x1b0 >= v,
* and _dn is x1ge{v} <== 1*x1b0 >= v.
@x1ge1_up @x1ge1_dn x1ge1 <==> 1 x1b0 >= 1 ;
* x1eq{v} means x1 = v, which is x1ge{v} and not x1ge{v+1}
* A conjunction is a pseudo-Boolean constraint too: asking for all
* of n literals is asking for their sum to be at least n.
@x1eq0_up @x1eq0_dn x1eq0 <==> 1 ~x1ge1 >= 1 ;
@x1eq1_up @x1eq1_dn x1eq1 <==> 1 x1ge1 >= 1 ;
*
* --- x2 in [0, 2], the model's x2 ---
* x2 = 2*x2b1 + 1*x2b0
@x2_ub 2 x2b1 1 x2b0 <= 2 ;
*
* x2ge{v} means x2 >= v, in both directions at once.
* Each line is two constraints: _up is x2ge{v} ==> 2*x2b1 + 1*x2b0 >= v,
* and _dn is x2ge{v} <== 2*x2b1 + 1*x2b0 >= v.
@x2ge1_up @x2ge1_dn x2ge1 <==> 2 x2b1 1 x2b0 >= 1 ;
@x2ge2_up @x2ge2_dn x2ge2 <==> 2 x2b1 1 x2b0 >= 2 ;
* x2eq{v} means x2 = v, which is x2ge{v} and not x2ge{v+1}
* A conjunction is a pseudo-Boolean constraint too: asking for all
* of n literals is asking for their sum to be at least n.
@x2eq0_up @x2eq0_dn x2eq0 <==> 1 ~x2ge1 >= 1 ;
@x2eq1_up @x2eq1_dn x2eq1 <==> 1 x2ge1 1 ~x2ge2 >= 2 ;
@x2eq2_up @x2eq2_dn x2eq2 <==> 1 x2ge2 >= 1 ;
*
* --- x3 in [0, 2], the model's x3 ---
* x3 = 2*x3b1 + 1*x3b0
@x3_ub 2 x3b1 1 x3b0 <= 2 ;
*
* x3ge{v} means x3 >= v, in both directions at once.
* Each line is two constraints: _up is x3ge{v} ==> 2*x3b1 + 1*x3b0 >= v,
* and _dn is x3ge{v} <== 2*x3b1 + 1*x3b0 >= v.
@x3ge1_up @x3ge1_dn x3ge1 <==> 2 x3b1 1 x3b0 >= 1 ;
@x3ge2_up @x3ge2_dn x3ge2 <==> 2 x3b1 1 x3b0 >= 2 ;
* x3eq{v} means x3 = v, which is x3ge{v} and not x3ge{v+1}
* A conjunction is a pseudo-Boolean constraint too: asking for all
* of n literals is asking for their sum to be at least n.
@x3eq0_up @x3eq0_dn x3eq0 <==> 1 ~x3ge1 >= 1 ;
@x3eq1_up @x3eq1_dn x3eq1 <==> 1 x3ge1 1 ~x3ge2 >= 2 ;
@x3eq2_up @x3eq2_dn x3eq2 <==> 1 x3ge2 >= 1 ;
*
* --- x4 in [0, 2], the model's x4 ---
* x4 = 2*x4b1 + 1*x4b0
@x4_ub 2 x4b1 1 x4b0 <= 2 ;
*
* x4ge{v} means x4 >= v, in both directions at once.
* Each line is two constraints: _up is x4ge{v} ==> 2*x4b1 + 1*x4b0 >= v,
* and _dn is x4ge{v} <== 2*x4b1 + 1*x4b0 >= v.
@x4ge1_up @x4ge1_dn x4ge1 <==> 2 x4b1 1 x4b0 >= 1 ;
@x4ge2_up @x4ge2_dn x4ge2 <==> 2 x4b1 1 x4b0 >= 2 ;
* x4eq{v} means x4 = v, which is x4ge{v} and not x4ge{v+1}
* A conjunction is a pseudo-Boolean constraint too: asking for all
* of n literals is asking for their sum to be at least n.
@x4eq0_up @x4eq0_dn x4eq0 <==> 1 ~x4ge1 >= 1 ;
@x4eq1_up @x4eq1_dn x4eq1 <==> 1 x4ge1 1 ~x4ge2 >= 2 ;
@x4eq2_up @x4eq2_dn x4eq2 <==> 1 x4ge2 >= 1 ;
*
* all_different(x2, x3, x4)
@amo1_0 1 x2eq0 1 x3eq0 1 x4eq0 <= 1 ;
@amo1_1 1 x2eq1 1 x3eq1 1 x4eq1 <= 1 ;
@amo1_2 1 x2eq2 1 x3eq2 1 x4eq2 <= 1 ;
*
* x1 + x2 + x3 + x4 <= 2
@lin2 1 x1b0 2 x2b1 1 x2b0 2 x3b1 1 x3b0 2 x4b1 1 x4b0 <= 2 ;
*
* - x1 + x2 + x3 + x4 <= 1
@lin3 -1 x1b0 2 x2b1 1 x2b0 2 x3b1 1 x3b0 2 x4b1 1 x4b0 <= 1 ;
